  "definition": "Microgravity is a condition in which a spacecraft and its occupants are in continuous free fall and experience very little sustained support acceleration. Gravity remains substantial in low Earth orbit; the apparent weightlessness arises because the vehicle, crew and equipment fall together. Drop towers and parabolic flights reproduce the condition for seconds, while orbiting laboratories provide exposure lasting months.[^1]",
